 Recursive Binary Search 

** Problem Statement
Find key usind recursion in a sorted array, found then retun index , else -1 . 

** Algorithm / Approach
Function khud ko sirf us half pe call karta hai jaha key ho sakti hai.
- **Base case 1:** `low > high` -> -1 (nahi mila).
- **Base case 2:** `arr[mid] == key` -> mid return.
- **Recursive case:** key badi hai to `(mid+1, high)`, chhoti hai to `(low, mid-1)`.

** Pseudocode

BINARY_SEARCH_RECURSIVE(arr, low, high, key):
    if low > high: return -1
    mid = low + (high - low) / 2
    if arr[mid] == key: return mid
    if arr[mid] < key:
        return BINARY_SEARCH_RECURSIVE(arr, mid + 1, high, key)
    else:
        return BINARY_SEARCH_RECURSIVE(arr, low, mid - 1, key)


** Time & Space Complexity 
Recurrence: `T(n) = T(n/2) + O(1)` -> **O(log n)** (Master Theorem).

| Case | Time |
|---|---|
| Best | O(1) |
| Average | O(log n) |
| Worst | O(log n) |
| **Space** | **O(log n)** (recursion stack depth) |




